    <PackageReleaseNotes>v6.8.0: Reactive context-overflow recovery. When the server rejects a request for exceeding the model's context window, the conversation is compacted and the request re-sent — the limit is the server's to report, so nothing is estimated client-side. Providers translate the rejection into ContextLengthExceededException (non-streaming) or a context_length_exceeded-flagged error chunk (streaming); streaming recovers inside the round loop, replaying only the round that overflowed and keeping earlier rounds' tool results. Tunable via AIService.ContextRecoveryMaxRetries (default 1, 0 disables). Also fixed: compaction that could not shrink the request used to discover that only after billing a summary and deleting history (routine at the default MaxMessageCount of 20); the summarization request inherited the caller's AIRequestContext and had its prompt overwritten by RequestMessageOverride; recovery retried turns whose side-effecting tools had already run; the rewind baseline was captured per turn instead of per attempt; streams that gave up ended without their Completion chunk; Anthropic's "input length and `max_tokens` exceed context limit" wording went undetected; MessageChain.SendAsync and RetryLastMessageAsync bypassed recovery; Gemini's legacy streaming path threw untranslated errors. ChatBlock.RemoveFunctionMessages() joins MaxMessageCount as [Obsolete] for removal in v7.0. Requires Mythosia.AI.Abstractions v2.5.0.</PackageReleaseNotes>
